    <!-- What's new -->
    <string name="whats_new">What’s new</string>
    <string name="whats_new_title">What’s new in version %1$s</string>
    <string-array name="whats_new_items">
        <item>A video on a recipe: paste a YouTube, Instagram, TikTok or Facebook link and watch it on the recipe page. A recipe copied from a video post keeps its video.</item>
        <item>A calmer look: white and black pages with red only on the main buttons, and a word under every action icon.</item>
        <item>Reading a recipe from photos now writes the name, ingredients and steps for you, handwriting and Greek included.</item>
        <item>A reel whose caption has no recipe is listened to: the spoken recipe is written down for you.</item>
        <item>Imported recipes can be translated into your language on the phone: switch it on in Settings.</item>
        <item>Tags on recipes, and filters: total time, cooked or not, rating, and “what’s in my pantry”.</item>
        <item>Pin a recipe to the top, duplicate it, or print it, from the menu on its page.</item>
        <item>After cooking, the app asks “Did you cook it?” and keeps a photo of the result with each entry in the cooked log.</item>
        <item>Plan a recipe as breakfast, lunch, snack or dinner, and write a note for each day of the calendar.</item>
        <item>The shopping list can show this week only.</item>
    </string-array>
